reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:59:## 2. How `invoice_before_due` = 6 hours is actually applied
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:61:`arraysubs_get_invoice_hours_before_due()` converts value+unit → hours (`value*24` when unit = `days`): `arraysubs/src/functions/settings-helpers.php:735-745`. Site value: `6` + `hours` → **6**.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:68:   - `invoice_ts = (D + k) − lead*3600`
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:69:   - **Guard**: `if (invoice_ts <= time() && D+k > time()) return time() + 60;` — i.e. when you time-travel a due date to "6 h from now or less", the invoice job is queued for **now + 1 minute**, not in the past.
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:77:| Renewal WC order | `pending` (created) → `processing`/`completed` (paid) or `failed` (charge declined, `RenewalProcessor.php:594-597`) or `cancelled` (subscription cancelled for non-payment, `RenewalProcessor.php:258`) |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:78:| Subscription | `arraysubs-active` throughout invoice + first grace window → `arraysubs-on-hold` (sweep phase 1) → `arraysubs-cancelled` (sweep phase 2). Registered slugs: `arraysubs-pending`, `arraysubs-active`, `arraysubs-on-hold`, `arraysubs-cancelled`, `arraysubs-expired`, `arraysubs-trial` — `arraysubs/src/Features/Subscriptions/Services/SubscriptionCPT.php:94-156` |
reference/SLT-REF-01-renewal-timeline-offsets-from-next-payment-date-order-sub-st.md:84:For an automatic-payment subscription with auto-renew on, `EmailManager::on_renewal_invoice_created()` **returns without sending the renewal-invoice email** (`EmailManager.php:495-513`). So on Stripe the customer sees nothing at `D+k−6h`; the first mail is the payment-successful (or payment-failed) email at `D+k`. On bacs/cheque/cod or `_auto_renew='off'`, the invoice email *does* go out at `D+k−6h`.
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:6:# SLT-REF-03 — Failed renewal, retries, grace, cancellation (reference note)
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:43:**Retries are NOT spread** — `scheduleNextRetry()` calls `scheduleSingle()` directly with `time()+interval`, bypassing `RenewalScheduler::schedule()`. Only the invoice/charge/reminder legs get the crc32 offset (`renewal-spread-helpers.php:26-30`).
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:58:## 4. Grace math mapped to real timestamps (this site: on_hold=1, cancel=3)
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:60:Helpers: `arraysubs_get_grace_days_before_on_hold()` `settings-helpers.php:714-717` (default 3 in code, **1 on this site**); `arraysubs_get_grace_days_before_cancel()` `:724-727` (default 7 in code, **3 on this site**).
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:68:- **Requires an unpaid renewal order to already exist.** If `hasUnpaidRenewalOrder()` is false the sweep *creates the invoice and `continue`s* — the subscription is **not** put on hold on that pass (`:673-678`).
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:76:- SQL cutoff `cancel_cutoff = gmdate(now − (1 + 3) = 4 days)`; selects `post_status = arraysubs-on-hold AND _next_payment_date < cutoff` (`:718-726`).
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:79:- `RenewalProcessor::cancelOverdueSubscription()` (`:756`, impl `RenewalProcessor.php:139-174`): status → `arraysubs-cancelled`; `_end_date`, `_cancelled_date` = now; `_cancelled_by = 'system'`; `_cancellation_reason = 'overdue_payment'`; cancels every unpaid renewal order (`cancelPendingRenewalOrders()` `:182-263`); `RenewalScheduler::unschedule()`; `do_action('arraysubs_data_cancelled_overdue')`.
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:81:**Effective cancel moment** = `max(D + 4 days, on_hold_date + 3 days)`, rounded up to the next hourly sweep. Because on-hold lands at ≈ D+24h, both terms coincide at **≈ D + 4 days**.
reference/SLT-REF-03-failed-renewal-retry-schedule-attempt-count-grace-day-timest.md:83:### Phase 3 — end-of-period cancellations (`processWaitingCancellationBatch()` `Hooks.php:770-818`)
